.TH "ROARK\-AGENT\-CONFIG\-UPDATE" "1" "" "roark-agent-config-update" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-agent\-config\-update \- Write a config revision
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark agent\-config update
\fIkey\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Write a new revision onto a channel. Writing production creates the key when it does not exist; writing staging stages a candidate that only Roark\-recognized simulation sessions will read. Every write is a new revision; nothing is overwritten.
.SH "API"
PUT /v1/agent\-config/{key}
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIkey\fR
The key.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-channel\fR \fI<value>\fR
Which channel to write. One of: production, staging. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-document\fR \fI<value>\fR
The full config JSON for the new revision. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\fR \fI<value>\fR
One\-line story of the change. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Link this config to a Roark agent (the one your calls report). Required before Autoimprove can run on it: the link is how a fix finds the config channel. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark agent\-config update <key> \-\-channel <value> \-\-document <value>
.fi
